WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight is
a Golden Globe-nominated actor

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from "Atonement"
and the "X-Man" franchise --

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:05.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"X-Men" franchise.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.074
He stars in M. Night Shyamalan's
new film "Glass,"

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is in theaters and IMAX
Friday.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:14.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know this seems
very unfair to you.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Pbht!

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:18.585 line:92%
-But you are stuck in this room.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's right there!

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.055 line:92%
You can't beat the beast!

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
He don't think you can beat
the beast, does he?

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Huh?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
Beast like --
[ Grunts ]

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't think he can beat
the beast, does he?

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.570
-Please welcome back to the show
James McAvoy, everyone!

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.806 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:56.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Welcome back.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do the guys keep playing
until I sit down?

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.659 line:92%
-Yeah, they would play forever.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Play until they starve.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had someone come once
who never sat down.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.600
It was really rough.
It was like a hostage situation.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.369
So, congratulations on the film.
-Thank you.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:14.307
-That was just one of I believe
20 different personalities

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.141 line:92%
your character has in this film.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.011 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, no, we had 23
in the original script,

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.546 line:92%
and then in the editing process,

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
Night decided to cut
three of them.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.283 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know why.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was all for
leave no personality behind.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, they ditched three
of them.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have to imagine you can't
approach this the way

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
you approach other roles
in terms of how you rehearse.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, err, no.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.367
-You know, typically on a movie,
even if it's a big movie,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.904
you get one week's rehearsal, so
trying to rehearse 20 characters

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:45.905 size:81% position:41% line:92%
was onerous, you know?

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:50.410
But actually, there was just a
lot of rehearsing in the mirror.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I've not done
since I was about 21.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.314
But there was a lot of just kind
of going like,

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
"All right,
that's how she looks.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.618
And, like, that's how he looks.
And then he's like this."

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.888
And it was kind of fun. I felt
like a kid again a little bit.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.589 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I would also imagine,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.391
on top of having to keep all
those personalities straight,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously this is
an M. Night movie.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're kind of famous for
their twists and turns,

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.398
where you also plot-wise have to
keep a lot of things straight.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:16.202 size:88% position:44%
Were you just sort of in
an utter confusion cloud

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the whole time, yeah?
-To be honest, yes.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:20.273 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On the first movie, "Split,"
he --

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.244
I got the script and I read it.
I loved it and all that.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.380
And you know, ultimately, we
revealed that it was linked to

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.681 line:92%
the world of "Unbreakable"

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.718
and Bruce Willis and
Samuel L. Jackson and all that.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.987 line:92%
I missed this completely.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:34.521 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, and their movie
that they made 19 years ago,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Unbreakable."

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.926 line:92%
And so we're like two weeks in,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.262
and I'm sitting there thinking,
like, geez --

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:46.166
"M. Night Shyamalan really talks
about 'Unbreakable' a lot."

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.334 line:92%
And I'm like -- no, dude.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.970
I'm not here going, like,
"Oh, I was in 'Atonement.'"

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.338 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.507 line:92%
You know, back on "Narnia..."

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:58.745
I'm like -- And then one day
he got really overt with it

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it -- kind of
the penny dropped,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.549
and I was like, "Oh! I get it."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.418
And I styled it out and I
pretended that I knew all along.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
It turns out this is why
it's very helpful

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:08.821 line:92%
when sequels are just the name

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the first movie
with a "2" after it.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, I know, yeah.
Exactly.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.060 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Then you don't miss it.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get to work with
two incredibly iconic co-stars

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.332
in Bruce Willis and Sam Jackson.
What was that like?

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, those gu--
I've worked with movie stars,

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people that are
my contemporaries

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.738
may be slightly older or
slightly younger, and it's cool.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.575
You know, but working with
those guys -- Bruce was --

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.311
Bruce was a movie star and
a big TV star when I was a kid.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember watching
"Moonlighting."

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-With him and Cybill Shepherd.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.648 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I loved him in that.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:39.986
And he made me laugh, he excited
me, he, like, terrified me.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.753 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was amazing.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.289 line:92%
And then Sam, more in my teens,

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.659
just watching him being
so dexterous as an actor.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:50.597
He's been an example, like,
for as long as I can remember

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:51.631 line:92%
even thinking about acting.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
Getting to work with him
was incredible.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.035
I remember we did this big
scene, a big long pink room

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we do, like,
a community therapy session.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a chair there,
we've got Bruce,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then a chair there,
we've got Sam,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a big long walk to
my empty chair in the middle.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:08.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's, like, weird --
and I'm walking down,

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.717 line:92%
and I sit down and I'm like,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
"All right, Sam.
All right, Bruce."

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:13.419 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.888
And then he says -- and then
the director says, "Action."

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:16.723 line:92%
I'm like -- I says, you know,

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:19.292
it's kind of a sort of pinch
yourself moment, you know?

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.562
-And you also got to do
a fair amount of press with Sam.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:25.865
Did you learn anything about
promoting a film from Sam?

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.368
-I mean, I saw examples of
what I might be able to do

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I've got the balls
that he's got.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
you've got to be --

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.411
That guy does not suffer fools,
which is a positive quality.

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.912 line:92%
But he gets any kind of question

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is in any way
not thought out properly,

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
he just drops the F-bomb
and he is like,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you talking about?
What? What?"

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.923
He calls them out so hard,
and it's the funniest thing.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did an interview
back in the U.K.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:56.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Lorraine Kelly,
who is a brilliant host.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it just didn't work out
with Sam and her.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm sitting there going --
and I've been on her show

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.836 size:84% position:42%
back home, like, many,
many, many, many times.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.238 line:92%
She's a lovely, lovely lady.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm sitting there
going, like,

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, no, this is going
real bad."

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.710
"This is going real --"
And I can't get in between them

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.379
because once he gets going,
there's no stopping him.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.147 line:92%
-Yeah. I think that's so.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:14.981 line:92%
-He's amazing. I love the guy.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:17.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want -- you know, I hope
when I'm his age --

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope when I'm --
a year from now I'm like him.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.722 line:92%
-Yeah, it's really fun, too.

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, earned confidence.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:28.361
-But a confidence must be a
delight to go through life with.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:30.697 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, for real.

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
You shot in
an abandoned hospital.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.335 line:92%
That was your actual set. Yes?

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:38.237
-Yeah, they abandoned it
because it was terrifying.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was too scary
to be a hospital.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was too --
it was a mental hospital,

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was making the patients
be mental.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:45.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it was a pretty scary
little joint.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:48.948 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And it was freezing.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:49.949 line:92%
And they turned the heating off.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we filmed it in, I think,
November in Pennsylvania,

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.154 size:75% position:38% line:92%
where it's freezing.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.157
And I'm running about with
no shoes on and no top on.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:02.261
And I'm like, "Night, why did
you write this for me right now?

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do like my nipples."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:07.300 size:84% position:42%
"I don't really want to
have them sewn back on

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
by some incredible
foreign surgeon

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.704 line:92%
I have to fly to and see."

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.273 line:92%
So, yeah, it was pretty gnarly.

